Redis is a type of database service that stores data directly in the computer's main memory (RAM), rather than on a hard drive (databases that stores directly in the RAM is called a In Memory database)  (while Traditional Database are stored Secondary memory) 

	• In this machine its running on port 6379 


	• We can use the utility redis-cli  to interact with REDIS databases on other machines 

		○ We need to put the command/flag -h to specify the host ip address
		
			redis-cli -h ipaddress
			
			
		○ Once inside we can use info to get the information about the database 
	
		○ We can use the command Select pick the needed database in Redis 
		○ KEY * to view the keys in it (it will show all the keys and if theres a lot might make the sever lag) 
		○ we get do TYPE keyname to view the type of the key, then based on that use the command needed to key content 
			
			For strings: GET keyname
			For lists: LRANGE keyname 0 -1
			For sets: SMEMBERS keyname
			For hashes: HGETALL keyname
			For sorted sets: ZRANGE keyname 0 -1 WITHSCORES
		
